{"title":"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Quick_Insight)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Quick Insight)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(I_didn&#39;t_know_Solution_1!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (I didn't know Solution 1!)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Remark_3.0.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark 3.0.1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(No_usage_of_initial_term_or_difference)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (No usage of initial term or difference)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀_Solved_in_5_min_🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀 Solved in 5 min 🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_By_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution By SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> be the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms of an arithmetic sequence that has a common difference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The quotient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/03568c99de5ca3c8b879a54c9c3e6a407f4b7ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"33\" height=\"42\" /> does not depend on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a171b62f8fa798757e7afa0ca4bbab5c2adeee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204f093c5940fdedc8baabb63a3823d0c027671d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 340 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 360 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 380 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 400 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"446\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's say that our sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/6949385de927daa2c0a1ca2865fa033d023d5684.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a, a+2, a+4, a+6, a+8, a+10, \\ldots.\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"15\" />\nThen, since the value of n doesn't matter in the quotient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/03568c99de5ca3c8b879a54c9c3e6a407f4b7ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"33\" height=\"42\" />, we can say that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211d4a410ea2f4e0fbb5ba5b4cfd339a58f3b8f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{S_{3}}{S_1} = \\frac{S_{6}}{S_2}.\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"40\" />\nSimplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5c4b32a201185302b576cd0c51c958b6d5719c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3a+6}{a}=\\frac{6a+30}{2a+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"143\" height=\"40\" />, from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b50f89c009267fd328dfb139693cfd6a8a6d21f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3a+6}{a}=\\frac{3a+15}{a+1}.\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/7/867df6bd88334ac5b0f1459607cc2e620226e9d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a^2+9a+6=3a^2+15a\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c88b943f424efaec2dad7f36bbe4f1effae81a16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6a=6\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> \nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Since the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> odd numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/9109a0feb9c12e94646be612d3e6b4143dbf0cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{20} = 20^2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Note: you could also plug in the formulas for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e86695d4207c9ac906f305891282131bc2a05f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"33\" height=\"42\" /> and simplify, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62036e426552bc355b658f154fbfda38b5d382a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+ \\frac{6n}{a+n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"111\" height=\"40\" /> You would then find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />\n~megacleverstarfish15\n</p><p><br />\n(Optimal competition solution if you're short on time.\n~Lunar Paradox)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the first term of the arithmetic sequence be \\(a_1\\), common difference \\(d=2\\).\n</p><p>The sum of first n terms of an arithmetic sequence:\n</p><p>\\(S_n=\\frac{n}{2}\\big[2a_1+(n-1)d\\big]\\)\nSubstitute \\(d=2\\):\n</p><p>\\(\\begin{align*}\nS_n&amp;=\\frac{n}{2}\\big[2a_1+2(n-1)\\big] \\\\\n&amp;=n\\big[a_1+n-1\\big] \\\\\n&amp;=n^2+(a_1-1)n\n\\end{align*}\\)Replace n with 3n:\n</p><p>\\(S_{3n}=(3n)^2+(a_1-1)(3n)=9n^2+3(a_1-1)n\\)Compute the ratio:\n</p><p>\\(\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}=\\frac{9n^2+3(a_1-1)n}{n^2+(a_1-1)n}=\\frac{9n+3(a_1-1)}{n+(a_1-1)}\\)This quotient is independent of n.\nFor the fraction \\(\\frac{9n+3(a_1-1)}{n+(a_1-1)}\\) to have no n dependence, the constant term in the numerator must be 9 times the constant term in the denominator.\n</p><p>\\(3(a_1-1)=9(a_1-1)\\)\n\\(6(a_1-1)=0 \\implies a_1=1\\)So \\(S_n=n^2\\).\n</p><p>\\(S_{20}=20^2=400\\)**Answer: D**\n</p><p>~Eddybai\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Quick_Insight.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Quick_Insight)\">Solution 2 (Quick Insight)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Quick Insight)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall that the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> odd numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f31002ad1c2d37f17438926da92b639a3bc74b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_{n}} = \\frac{9n^2}{n^2} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"122\" height=\"44\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/9109a0feb9c12e94646be612d3e6b4143dbf0cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{20} = 20^2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~numerophile\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28I_didn.27t_know_Solution_1.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(I_didn't_know_Solution_1!)\">Solution 3 (I didn't know Solution 1!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (I didn&#39;t know Solution 1!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have a slightly challenging problem&#160;:-(, but that's okay!\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/8249f238c6dc1f21360d7da6cd950e148bfb2360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{If you didn&#39;t come up with the Solution 1 intuition}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"430\" height=\"17\" />, then here is a more direct approach.\n</p><p>We want \\(\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}\\) to be a natural (\\(\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n} &gt; 0\\); basically a whole number \\(\\neq 0\\)) number. Then only can the progression be incremental by 2.\n</p><p>Assume that \\(a_1 = 1\\). Then, \\(a_2 = 3\\), \\(a_3 = 5\\), etc. We take the first term \\(n=1\\), which is 1. Then \\(3n\\); the next 3 terms will sum to 9. \\(\\frac{9}{1} = 9\\), and this is an arithmetic sequence, and therefore works!\n</p><p>What about \\(a_1 = 0\\). We immediately see that this would be undefined, so we cannot have \\(a_1 = 0\\). So we say \\(a_1 = 2\\). Then the sum for \\(n=1\\) is  2, and for \\(3n\\); it is simply 6. This is \\(6/2 = 3\\), so it works!\n</p><p>Then, what about \\(a_2 = 3\\)? Then this means that the \\(n=2\\) sum is 4, and the \\(3n\\) sum is 36. This is \\(36/4 = 9\\), and this is the same as the difference before, proving that \\(a_1 = 1\\) is indeed correct.\n</p><p>And then? What about \\(a_2 = 4\\)? This means \\(n=2\\) sum is 6, and the \\(3n\\) sum is 42, but uh oh, the progression breaks! Therefore, the evens cannot work.\n</p><p>Therefore, \\(a_1 = 1\\), \\(a_{20}\\) is just the sum of the first 20 odd numbers, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87ba0a41d515f1f1c169aa09ed4d176e1b87255b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark_3.0.1\">Remark 3.0.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Remark 3.0.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Hi! It me (Pinotation) again!\n</p><p>If you are confused about why \\( a_1 \\neq 3 \\) or \\( a_1 \\neq 4 \\) or something along those lines, we can prove by induction.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a60f58314503a8afc3fb95fc1111d4805c50b75.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_n=\\frac{n}{2}\\big(2a_1+(n-1)\\cdot 2\\big)=n(a_1+n-1).\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"32\" />\nThen\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/2696c5754a7220b32cdbc20463d7ac272c0028eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_{3n}=3n(a_1+3n-1),\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/1029f216fbeb7df4df1cec53d1f154d535beab5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}=\\frac{3(a_1+3n-1)}{a_1+n-1}.\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Base case \\( n=1 \\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee72ce40d8db129332fc937f9263877e899e6f86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{S_3}{S_1}=\\frac{3(a_1+2)}{a_1}.\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Suppose for some \\( n \\) the ratio is independent of \\( n \\) and equal to a constant \\( k \\). Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/2/862594fe06a183f837c7caae6a603126e334cc2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}=\\frac{3(a_1+3n-1)}{a_1+n-1}=k.\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"41\" />\nFor \\( n+1 \\) we must also have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4be346af7a2aa1f94c29874a300b59d77cf5c5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{S_{3(n+1)}}{S_{n+1}}=\\frac{3(a_1+3n+2)}{a_1+n}=k.\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"42\" />\nSo\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a334ec8d971590581285452200512b2cd16c03a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3(a_1+3n-1)}{a_1+n-1}=\\frac{3(a_1+3n+2)}{a_1+n}.\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"41\" />\nCross multiplying gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21eeef50c5666a49717171b2e4fbf8af006c6fb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1+3n-1)(a_1+n)=(a_1+3n+2)(a_1+n-1).\\]\" width=\"395\" height=\"18\" />\nExpanding,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b6afac16b138ff3075f803437cbf010ccf1370.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1^2+4na_1+a_1- n -3 = a_1^2+4na_1+a_1+2n-2.\\]\" width=\"396\" height=\"20\" />\nSimplifying,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e369acf1ed291642109df2cf14c6a6708bfe767d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[- n -3 = 2n -2,\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b787e74da8d4eb14f946871c6049987b04b843b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3n = -1.\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />\nThis is impossible for integer \\( n \\). The only way the equality can hold for all \\( n \\) is if the proportionality factor between numerator and denominator is fixed. Comparing coefficients in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/48930986cc526e7075e46ba97a8eae83d05e6f76.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3(a_1+3n-1)=C(a_1+n-1),\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" />\nwe get \\( C=9 \\) and hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f2fd9759e39e91db4b5ccbe2ee7c201b690191f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a_1-3=9a_1-9 \\implies a_1=1.\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>I hope this helped! If not, then you can check Solution 1, as it is practically the friendlier version LOL!\n</p><p>~Proof by Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the first element. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4140a64c736dcb7095b9e818a33c9b5be5a6e46d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{20}=20(a+19)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />. Let it equal to all the answer choices respectively, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80aacb0459953061b8d18065255c7d00f0d7356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-2, -1, 0, 1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"17\" />. We test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/03568c99de5ca3c8b879a54c9c3e6a407f4b7ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"33\" height=\"42\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/2421fa2bd0f312bb9910b9f099afdc9026a7ff5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />. We can see that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f8bac155a0878c828c3ee23a27ca8db0b31528d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-2, -1, 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" /> there exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/852bc67814f5a59c0344d8961732b040eaa0508b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />, which implies they are invalid. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> we can also see it's invalid, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/9255cea386483cff471f60788039d7814ca7f527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S_3}{S_1}=6\\neq7=\\frac{S_6}{S_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"138\" height=\"42\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87ba0a41d515f1f1c169aa09ed4d176e1b87255b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" /> is the correct choice.\n</p><p>~metrixgo\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28No_usage_of_initial_term_or_difference.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(No_usage_of_initial_term_or_difference)\">Solution 5 (No usage of initial term or difference)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (No usage of initial term or difference)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a and d be the initial term and difference respectively. (These won't be used it later)\n</p><p>Notice that the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a72796fb8f79243b80b5c042f8fb6a6793f7fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1,n+2,...,2n=(a+d+nd),(a+2d+nd),...,(a+nd+nd)=S_{n}+n(nd)=S_{n}+n^2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"730\" height=\"21\" />. In a similar fashion, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b1f718964c8a536470e4367031a4beb0c60ca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{3n}=3S_{n}+2n^2+4n^2=3S_{n}+6n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"285\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We are given that the quotient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/03568c99de5ca3c8b879a54c9c3e6a407f4b7ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"33\" height=\"42\" /> does not depend on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. With the result above, we have  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e7f11592f0cde0d665537908cd94d30ebbeab5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3S_{n}+6n^2}{S_n}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"42\" />\nwhere we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fecc3490d7bd8615c25cc6c902bd9aa0a91e8184.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3+\\frac{6n^2}{S_n}\\]\" width=\"60\" height=\"42\" />\nWith the information above, we must have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9f125e082d9566d84abaf65b1712882126ff7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_{n}=kn^2\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c36f13a3a5584652df1fad4716d137a0617e2af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\neq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/96766aa44d8c0fc2b2a1129d0acbade102605a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${d\\neq2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2a420978db58ced573fc7c70407472b315fcbc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n}=n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d43e515de3ab8cca5174da27410dace3c64e0e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{20}=20^2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p>~kobers\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.F0.9F.9A.80_Solved_in_5_min_.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(🚀_Solved_in_5_min_🚀)\">Video Solution (🚀 Solved in 5 min 🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (🚀 Solved in 5 min 🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7ztNpblm2TY\">https://youtu.be/7ztNpblm2TY</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_By_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution By SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution By SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zHJJyMlH9DA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zHJJyMlH9DA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qkyRBpQHbOA\">https://youtu.be/qkyRBpQHbOA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Mi2AxPhnRno?t=1299\">https://youtu.be/Mi2AxPhnRno?t=1299</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Ani_lytical\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/muBlEEUwei8?si=ovyiRgAlSVQvHelc\">https://youtu.be/muBlEEUwei8?si=ovyiRgAlSVQvHelc</a>\n</p><p>~Ani_lytical\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B\">2022 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2022 A